1
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:44,920
(Phone call ends)

2
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,240
(Chirping)

3
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:46,740
(Chirping)

4
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:48,480
Look at that!

5
00:01:48,494 --> 00:01:51,360
All right, good. Now stand to the right of the tree.

6
00:01:51,719 --> 00:01:52,840
All right, around here?

7
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:56,340
Yeah, get closer to the tree. A little more to the left.

8
00:01:58,259 --> 00:01:59,360
Around here?

9
00:02:00,014 --> 00:02:01,520
All right, right there. Good.

10
00:02:01,979 --> 00:02:03,700
Come on, let's wrap this up quickly.

11
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,600
What on earth are they doing?

12
00:02:07,274 --> 00:02:10,660
They seem to be peering through something. What can you see, Mr. Earthworm?

13
00:02:11,849 --> 00:02:15,640
Oh, I can't see a thing until nightfall.

14
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:18,660
I've got a bad feeling about this.

15
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:22,260
Listen, my babies are about to hatch. What if something happens?

16
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,960
I've seen that before. They're surveying the land.

17
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:29,200
What do they plan on doing once it's surveyed?

18
00:02:29,385 --> 00:02:30,385
Beats me!

19
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:37,240
Hmm, that really is a massive tree.

20
00:02:37,464 --> 00:02:39,680
Heheh, you're so right, Boss.

21
00:02:40,325 --> 00:02:42,180
Hmm, that tree really bothers me.

22
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:43,340
I know!

23
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:58,240
Cricket is my friend, hehe, we're the best of pals~

24
00:02:58,241 --> 00:02:59,300
Mokku, you're good at that~

25
00:02:59,301 --> 00:03:02,400
But, but... Hey, Mokku!

26
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:05,620
Good morning!

27
00:03:05,739 --> 00:03:07,900
Mokku, could you come here for a second?

28
00:03:08,225 --> 00:03:12,880
No way, I'm heading to school. I don't have time to dilly-dally.

29
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:17,200
I know, but it won't take long. Please!

30
00:03:17,555 --> 00:03:21,860
I have to be a good boy if I want to become human. Don't tempt me.

31
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,660
It's hard enough for me to stay on track as it is.

32
00:03:25,134 --> 00:03:29,820
Some human adults gathered around the Oak Tree, and they're doing something strange.

33
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:33,040
What? Around the Oak Tree?

34
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:36,980
I have a bad feeling something awful is about to happen.

35
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,340
What on earth are they trying to do?

36
00:03:40,804 --> 00:03:42,860
Please, go find out what's going on.

37
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:45,440
I can't understand human speech.

38
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:48,860
You say you've got a bad feeling?

39
00:03:49,269 --> 00:03:50,320
All right, I'll go.

40
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:52,280
Thanks, Mokku. Let's go!

41
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,400
All right!

42
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:55,260
Mokku...

43
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:03,620
Mokku is actually trying to do something to help Giorgio today.

44
00:04:03,984 --> 00:04:07,400
Well, I won't scold him for straying this time. Let's just see how this plays out.

45
00:04:11,024 --> 00:04:13,500
Huh? Aren't they just surveying the land?

46
00:04:14,119 --> 00:04:16,399
The one setting up the pole is Franco's dad.

47
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,459
I know that.

48
00:04:18,710 --> 00:04:24,580
You want to know what on earth they're doing that for, right? Got it. I'll go ask for you.

49
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,740
Franco's dad, good morning!

50
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:33,560
Franco's dad!

51
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:35,170
What?

52
00:04:35,925 --> 00:04:39,040
Oh, it's Mokku. What are you measuring this place for?

53
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:39,840
Huh?

54
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,160
What's this?

55
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:43,060
Hey! What are you peeking at?!

56
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,300
This isn't for kids to see!

57
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:52,780
Fix my neck, my neck! Boss, shall we head down the mountain soon?

58
00:04:59,810 --> 00:05:00,920
Huh, they left.

59
00:05:04,910 --> 00:05:06,980
Hey, Mokku. Did you find out?

60
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,440
No, no good.

61
00:05:08,925 --> 00:05:10,940
And you were our only hope.

62
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,740
Aw, don't look so sad.

63
00:05:14,265 --> 00:05:16,800
I know, I'll ask Franco. All right?

64
00:05:20,935 --> 00:05:22,220
Is that true, Franco?

65
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:23,840
Yeah, it's true.

66
00:05:24,165 --> 00:05:26,320
I heard Dad talking to Mom about it last night.

67
00:05:26,905 --> 00:05:29,180
It's gonna be great once the amusement park is built!

68
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:33,340
But Franco, what on earth is an amusement park?

69
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:35,860
It's a playground for kids like us.

70
00:05:36,125 --> 00:05:39,100
They're building an amusement park with all kinds of rides.

71
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,080
It's gonna be amazing!

72
00:05:41,230 --> 00:05:45,660
It's a kids' paradise, with a carousel, a Ferris wheel, and tons of rides!

73
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:17,140
[[NO AUDIO]]

74
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:20,660
Wow, that sounds like it'll be a lot of fun.

75
00:06:21,045 --> 00:06:24,640
Come on, you'll get to play there every day, so you must be looking forward to it, too.

76
00:06:25,145 --> 00:06:26,680
Yeah, I hope it's finished soon.

77
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:32,880
Hey, Franco, tell your dad to hurry up and build it! / Sure, will do. I'll tell him.

78
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:37,120
Franco's dad is really amazing.

79
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:39,260
You bet he is!

80
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:41,980
Huh? An amusement park here?

81
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:45,680
It's the quietest place in the village, with the best view.

82
00:06:45,930 --> 00:06:49,680
They say they're building a huge one, with tons of things to play on.

83
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,380
But this Oak Tree will be all right, won't it, Mokku?

84
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:55,420
Huh?

85
00:06:55,825 --> 00:06:59,180
That's right. They wouldn't cut it down, would they?

86
00:06:59,575 --> 00:07:03,760
Well... I didn't ask about that.

87
00:07:04,010 --> 00:07:09,980
What if it gets chopped down? What will we do? We won't have anywhere to live!

88
00:07:10,115 --> 00:07:12,640
Mokku, that's not going to happen, right?

89
00:07:12,915 --> 00:07:16,700
Don't ask me. It's not like I'm the one building it.

90
00:07:17,419 --> 00:07:19,540
Mokku, this affects you, too!

91
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:25,660
It's useless if you don't ask the most important thing! Hurry up and find out!

92
00:07:25,895 --> 00:07:30,980
B-But... Just go! If you dawdle, I'll poke your butt like last time!

93
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:34,520
A-All right, I get it! Mokku, hurry up, hurry!

94
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,040
Quit dragging your feet!

95
00:07:36,215 --> 00:07:37,780
I'm going, I'm going!

96
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:39,640
We're counting on you, Mokku!

97
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:44,320
I wonder if Mokku will be okay. He doesn't seem very reliable.

98
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:48,800
Man, that scared me. Why does everyone get so worked up?

99
00:07:52,885 --> 00:07:56,160
Ugh, I got dirt in my mouth. Geez.

100
00:07:57,235 --> 00:08:01,860
Why do I have to rush around like this? Give me a break.

101
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:05,520
Oh no, look what I did.

102
00:08:08,085 --> 00:08:09,800
It has nothing to do with me anyway.

103
00:08:10,375 --> 00:08:14,180
Whether that Oak Tree gets chopped down or whatever happens to it, it's not my problem.

104
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:15,740
You idiot!

105
00:08:16,190 --> 00:08:17,260
You ungrateful brat!

106
00:08:18,010 --> 00:08:20,580
That Oak Tree is your mother!

107
00:08:20,945 --> 00:08:21,945
My mother?

108
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:22,940
Listen to me!

109
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:28,100
The Fairy who gave you life lives in that Oak Tree! You big fool!

110
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,400
The Fairy who gave me life...

111
00:08:37,709 --> 00:08:42,440
Mokku, I am the Fairy of the Oak Tree, your home.

112
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:49,040
I have heard Grandfather's wish, and I have come to give you life.

113
00:08:49,975 --> 00:08:54,540
Grant life to the wooden puppet, Mokku.

114
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,040
[[MUSIC]]

115
00:09:02,259 --> 00:09:10,160
And Mokku, do you remember? When you fell into this stream and were almost smashed to pieces in the waterfall basin...

116
00:09:10,749 --> 00:09:13,780
Who was it that reached out a hand to save you?

117
00:09:15,839 --> 00:09:17,520
Ha ha ha!

118
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:19,500
Look out!

119
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:20,800
Help me!

120
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,440
Hang in there, Mokku!

121
00:09:39,629 --> 00:09:41,620
Mokku, hold on!

122
00:09:42,929 --> 00:09:43,929
Be brave!

123
00:09:45,569 --> 00:09:48,000
If you give up over something like this, you can never become human.

124
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:50,860
Now, take heart and climb out.

125
00:09:56,739 --> 00:09:59,620
Do you really not care if that Oak Tree gets chopped down?

126
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:05,380
I'll ask Franco's dad to see if they're really going to cut down the Oak Tree.

127
00:10:05,895 --> 00:10:08,740
That's it, that's the spirit! I'm counting on you, Mokku.

128
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,960
Hey, wait up. I'm coming too.

129
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:17,840
Cheers!

130
00:10:17,870 --> 00:10:22,040
To celebrate the President's new project...

131
00:10:22,969 --> 00:10:30,160
I made a success of the coastal tourism business. This time, I'll make sure that mountain amusement park succeeds without fail!

132
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:45,140
Once it's built, huge crowds will be packing in! Which means money will come rolling in... Yes, I'll do anything for money! I have to build the amusement park as soon as possible!

133
00:10:47,019 --> 00:10:58,840
To do that, first we've gotta chop down that huge oak tree on top of the mountain! I knew it... Mokku! They really are going to cut down the Oak Tree! Are you just going to let them, Mokku?!

134
00:11:00,014 --> 00:11:03,920
The Oak Tree... The Oak Tree is going to be cut down...

135
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Stop!

136
00:11:11,025 --> 00:11:12,025
Stop!

137
00:11:16,279 --> 00:11:18,340
Stop! Stop!

138
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:34,760
Please stop!

139
00:11:39,089 --> 00:11:40,400
Ah!

140
00:11:41,889 --> 00:11:44,800
Stop it! Please stop!

141
00:12:08,209 --> 00:12:12,880
A dream...? Thank goodness it was just a dream...

142
00:12:24,419 --> 00:12:28,680
All right! I'll definitely protect that Oak Tree!

143
00:12:31,789 --> 00:12:39,540
I'm the village headman... did you come running to Silk Hat too?

144
00:12:39,905 --> 00:12:44,160
Um, Grandfather is back. Sorry, Koro-papa!

145
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:45,520
Huh?

146
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:47,200
Who is it?

147
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:48,840
Huh?

148
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:50,620
Me?

149
00:12:51,519 --> 00:12:53,900
There are two or three of you.

150
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:57,260
What is it? What do you want?

151
00:12:57,359 --> 00:13:00,720
Is it true they're building an amusement park on the Oak Tree's mountain?

152
00:13:01,055 --> 00:13:04,300
Yeah, that's right. And it's going to be something incredible.

153
00:13:04,665 --> 00:13:05,940
Could you please stop?

154
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:09,040
Huh? Yeah, sure, like I'd stop!

155
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:10,460
Wh-What?

156
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:16,580
That Oak Tree on my hill... I mean, all kinds of animals and insects live in that tree.

157
00:13:17,109 --> 00:13:19,600
So please, can't you leave it the way it is?

158
00:13:20,275 --> 00:13:21,460
Stop messing around!

159
00:13:22,609 --> 00:13:25,000
What kind of nonsense are you talking? Shut up!

160
00:13:25,165 --> 00:13:26,420
Give your stupidity a rest!

161
00:13:26,421 --> 00:13:28,060
Please. Stop it.

162
00:13:28,745 --> 00:13:29,780
Shut up!

163
00:13:30,014 --> 00:13:31,980
Please, listen to me! I'm begging you!

164
00:13:32,385 --> 00:13:33,980
Like hell we'll listen to that!

165
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,780
Ah! Mokku!

166
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,460
Ah!

167
00:13:38,290 --> 00:13:39,800
Oh, that's terrible.

168
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:41,300
Mokku, are you all right?

169
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:43,220
Spouting such nonsense.

170
00:13:45,109 --> 00:13:46,860
Come on, Mokku, pull yourself together!

171
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,760
Oh, no, he can't go to school like this.

172
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:52,220
What a cruel thing to do.

173
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:55,520
Now, if you've learned your lesson, hurry up and go home.

174
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:59,860
Giorgione!

175
00:13:59,861 --> 00:14:00,160
Hey!

176
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:05,360
Hey! Give my hat back!

177
00:14:05,665 --> 00:14:08,140
You little prankster, get down from there right now!

178
00:14:10,055 --> 00:14:13,520
Hyahaha! Serves you right!

179
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:16,280
Making a fool out of me... just watch what I'll do!

180
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,200
Go get it!

181
00:14:22,659 --> 00:14:25,340
Oh, tease him! This is fun!

182
00:14:32,039 --> 00:14:35,600
Look out! Giorgio, stop! Stop!

183
00:14:35,930 --> 00:14:37,320
Shut up!

184
00:14:42,229 --> 00:14:43,229
My hand...

185
00:14:44,509 --> 00:14:47,140
It snapped...

186
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:52,660
Ah!

187
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:56,740
Giorgio!

188
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,500
Giorgio!

189
00:14:59,789 --> 00:15:00,789
Hang in there!

190
00:15:04,629 --> 00:15:05,920
Serves you right!

191
00:15:11,139 --> 00:15:14,220
Grandpa, Giorgio will be able to fly again, won't he?

192
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:19,620
The injury isn't serious. He'll heal if he rests for a day or two.

193
00:15:20,179 --> 00:15:21,320
That's a relief, Giorgio.

194
00:15:21,745 --> 00:15:26,720
If the Oak Tree is going to be chopped down, who cares if my wings heal or not.

195
00:15:27,829 --> 00:15:29,440
What are you saying, Giorgio?

196
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:33,960
Because it's true! Everyone's home will be gone!

197
00:15:35,249 --> 00:15:37,500
There's no point in living like that.

198
00:15:38,405 --> 00:15:41,600
Now then, Mokku's hand... let's see.

199
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:47,980
Oh, that's right. I used up the rest of the oak wood when I fixed Mokku's leg the other day.

200
00:15:50,555 --> 00:15:55,000
Don't worry anymore. I'll go negotiate with Vittorio.

201
00:15:55,275 --> 00:15:57,000
Really, Grandpa?!

202
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:04,340
The plateau with that Oak Tree has the most beautiful view in the village.

203
00:16:04,735 --> 00:16:09,280
I am completely against building some gaudy playground in a place like that.

204
00:16:09,855 --> 00:16:12,820
The sensible villagers will surely oppose it too.

205
00:16:13,530 --> 00:16:16,260
We'll all stand together and protect the Oak Tree.

206
00:16:16,805 --> 00:16:18,060
Please do, Grandpa.

207
00:16:18,609 --> 00:16:20,500
Isn't that great, Giorgio?

208
00:16:20,665 --> 00:16:24,820
Yeah. I want to go tell the squirrels and wild birds right away.

209
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,640
Mokku, look, your arm is all finished.

210
00:16:28,425 --> 00:16:32,460
Being a wooden puppet makes you easy to repair, thankfully. There, how's that?

211
00:16:33,110 --> 00:16:34,160
Thank you, Grandpa.

212
00:16:35,209 --> 00:16:37,200
Huh, that's weird.

213
00:16:40,109 --> 00:16:41,240
What's wrong with it?

214
00:16:43,359 --> 00:16:44,980
Hm? What's the matter?

215
00:16:46,089 --> 00:16:48,980
Grandpa, it won't move like it used to.

216
00:16:49,245 --> 00:16:54,240
It isn't made of oak, so it probably won't move right away. Don't worry, it'll move once you get used to it.

217
00:16:54,725 --> 00:16:56,980
Well, I have to go talk to them.

218
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:59,180
I wonder...

219
00:17:02,689 --> 00:17:05,800
What the hell are you babbling about? An old geezer like you has no business interfering!

220
00:17:06,589 --> 00:17:09,980
Vitore, please. This is a peaceful mountain. I want you to leave it in peace.

221
00:17:10,244 --> 00:17:20,060
The mountain is far more beautiful as it is than with some amusement park. You just stick to your woodcarving, old man! Building a leisure land there is already a done deal. Now get lost!

222
00:17:20,904 --> 00:17:25,619
No matter how much you object, it won't change a thing, old man! B-But, Vitore!

223
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:42,680
Then there's really no saving the Oak Tree... Forgive me, it's all because I'm so powerless. Let us pray to God to protect the Oak Tree...

224
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:46,560
That's the only thing we can do right now.

225
00:17:52,199 --> 00:17:57,960
God, please protect the Oak Tree. Please hear my prayer.

226
00:18:17,099 --> 00:18:19,780
Hurry up and get ready! Do you have all the tools?

227
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:21,180
Yes!

228
00:18:25,139 --> 00:18:27,460
All right, let's begin! Cut that tree down!

229
00:18:31,414 --> 00:18:36,000
Ah, at last... has my final moment come...?

230
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:36,880
Huh?

231
00:18:36,881 --> 00:18:37,881
What?

232
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:44,560
Aaargh!

233
00:18:44,834 --> 00:18:46,060
Ah! It's Mokku!

234
00:18:46,939 --> 00:18:49,480
Stop it! Stop cutting down the Oak Tree!

235
00:18:49,764 --> 00:18:51,500
This is none of your business!

236
00:18:54,024 --> 00:18:56,480
Stop! Please, I'm begging you!

237
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:57,800
Get lost!

238
00:18:59,259 --> 00:19:02,440
Keep getting in our way and I'll smash you to pieces first!

239
00:19:03,124 --> 00:19:05,800
Hey! Wait! Stop! I beg of you!

240
00:19:05,801 --> 00:19:09,000
Listen here, old man! Get in our way again and you won't be spared!

241
00:19:09,429 --> 00:19:13,540
That's right, I have official permission from the town hall!

242
00:19:14,619 --> 00:19:19,320
Grandpa, if they cut down the Oak Tree, I'd rather die!

243
00:19:19,809 --> 00:19:21,540
All right, boys, get to it!

244
00:19:22,185 --> 00:19:23,185
Heave!

245
00:19:24,614 --> 00:19:26,420
Mokku, what are you saying?

246
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:30,420
But Grandpa, Mama... the Oak Tree is going to be cut down!

247
00:19:30,584 --> 00:19:33,860
Mokku, pray. Pray to God.

248
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:41,380
What are you muttering...? God! Please! Please save the Oak Tree!

249
00:19:41,994 --> 00:19:45,140
Please save the Oak Tree... Save my mother!

250
00:19:45,824 --> 00:19:49,240
I beg you! Take my life instead!

251
00:19:50,379 --> 00:19:54,220
Please... Please save my mother!

252
00:19:55,125 --> 00:19:56,125
Dear God!

253
00:19:56,779 --> 00:19:58,160
All right, let's do this!

254
00:19:58,161 --> 00:20:00,640
Go ahead.

255
00:20:01,024 --> 00:20:02,060
Dear God!

256
00:20:18,159 --> 00:20:19,600
God, please help us!

257
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:20,780
God, please help us!

258
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:23,800
God, please help us!

259
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:31,040
Help!

260
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:33,020
Forget it!

261
00:20:33,245 --> 00:20:34,760
Run!

262
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:39,640
Help!

263
00:20:41,789 --> 00:20:42,789
Brother!

264
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:48,060
Help me!

265
00:20:53,379 --> 00:20:54,380
Help me!

266
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,860
Somebody help me!

267
00:20:57,784 --> 00:21:00,260
Help me!

268
00:21:00,349 --> 00:21:02,660
Vittorio, take my hand!

269
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:05,580
Grandfather, you shouldn't help a guy like him!

270
00:21:06,175 --> 00:21:07,175
Fool!

271
00:21:08,719 --> 00:21:10,300
Come on, grab on, Vittorio!

272
00:21:11,089 --> 00:21:12,860
I-I'm sorry...

273
00:21:29,109 --> 00:21:31,260
Hold on, Mokku. Almost there.

274
00:21:39,624 --> 00:21:42,060
Thank you, Mokku. Thank you.

275
00:21:45,649 --> 00:21:47,940
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

276
00:21:49,974 --> 00:21:53,180
You did well, Mokku. Everything is all right now.

277
00:21:56,859 --> 00:21:59,040
Thank goodness! I'm so glad!

278
00:21:59,304 --> 00:22:00,820
It's all thanks to Mokku!

279
00:22:23,939 --> 00:22:26,780
Mokku, you did so well protecting the Oak Tree.

280
00:22:28,719 --> 00:22:31,860
Thank you. And you did well to help others with that disabled hand.

281
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:42,260
I will give you a reward. I shall transfer the life of the oak branch struck by lightning into this hand.

282
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:51,120
(Audio)

283
00:22:51,154 --> 00:22:53,560
Ah! It moves! It's moving!

284
00:22:54,529 --> 00:22:59,460
Grandpa! Grandpa! I-I-It's fixed! My left hand can move!

285
00:23:00,359 --> 00:23:02,260
Is that so? That's wonderful!

286
00:23:02,855 --> 00:23:06,560
The Fairy was right after all! It moves, Grandpa!

287
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:12,580
Because you tried so hard to protect the Oak Tree, God healed it for you.

288
00:23:14,499 --> 00:23:18,160
If only you were always a good boy like this, I wouldn't have such a hard time.

289
00:23:19,569 --> 00:23:24,800
Mokku is gradually becoming a good boy. (laughter)

290
00:23:33,569 --> 00:23:40,300
Learning that Mokku is at his wit's end after insects ate one of his legs, Kenken and his gang hatch another evil scheme.

291
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:45,400
In exchange for telling him who can fix his leg, they tell him to break the embankment.

292
00:23:46,439 --> 00:23:49,760
Suspecting nothing, Mokku is tricked into throwing stones at the embankment.

293
00:23:52,199 --> 00:23:53,980
And that night, heavy rain begins to fall,

294
00:23:54,234 --> 00:23:57,800
and an overflowing torrent of water violently assaults the embankment.

295
00:23:58,984 --> 00:24:01,400
Look forward to next week's episode of Kashi no Ki Mokku.

